#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179512 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "2574b91a-6534-562b-b4dc-8d95fd19e169" :question/math-academy-id "e-9480" :question/problem "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5]$. If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}$, calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j$." :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n∑_(j = 1)^(n)3Δy_{j} = 3∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nis just the length of the interval $[-3, 5]$, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j} &= Δy_{1} + Δy_{2} + Δy_{3} + ⋯ + Δy_{n} \\\\\n&= (y_{1} - y_{0}) + (y_{2} - y_{1}) + (y_{3} - y_{2}) + ⋯ + (y_{n} - y_{n - 1}) \\\\\n&= (y_{1} - y_{0}) + (y_{2} - y_{1}) + (y_{3} - y_{2}) + ⋯ + (y_{n} - y_{n - 1}) \\\\\n&=-y_{0} + y_{n} \\\\\n&= y_{n} - y_{0} \\\\\n&= 5 - (-3) \\\\\n&= 5 + 3 \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179513 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "8f09771b-3e0d-567b-a39f-f877bff53372" :question/math-academy-id "e-9481" :question/problem "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4]$. If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$, calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i$." :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)(x_{i} + x_{i - 1})Δx_{i} &= (x_{1} + x_{0})Δx_{1} + (x_{2} + x_{1})Δx_{2} + ⋯ + (x_{m} + x_{m - 1})Δx_{m} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{0})(x_{1} - x_{0}) + (x_{2} + x_{1})(x_{2} - x_{1}) + ⋯ + (x_{m} + x_{m - 1})(x_{m} - x_{m - 1}) \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}) + (x_{2}^{2} - x_{1}^{2}) + ⋯ + (x_{m}^{2} - x_{m - 1}^{2}) \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}) + (x_{2}^{2} - x_{1}^{2}) + ⋯ + (x_{m}^{2} - x_{m - 1}^{2}) \\\\\n&=-x_{0}^{2} + x_{m}^{2} \\\\\n&= x_{m}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)(x_{i} + x_{i - 1})Δx_{i} &= x_{m}^{2} - x_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= 4^{2} - (-3)^{2} \\\\\n&= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179515 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "eff8c72f-429d-583a-aa22-f7786f09262a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9484" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]$?\n\n1. $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n2. $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n3. $1 < 2 < 9$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 < x_1< x_2 < \\ldots < x_n = b\\,\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9$.\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9]$.\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9]$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d630d77c-ba48-5a29-9e49-615ab8a60c89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186